@startuml
!theme plain
title Mandatory Host Trust Before Authentication

actor User
participant "Containing App" as App
database "Versioned Profile Store" as Profiles
participant "Packet Tunnel Provider" as Provider
participant "Host Identity Policy" as Policy
database "Shared Keychain" as Keychain
participant "User-owned SSH Host" as Host

User -> App : Connect selected profile
App -> Provider : Start(profileID, generation)
Provider -> Profiles : Load immutable non-secret snapshot
Provider -> Host : Open transport and receive server host key
Provider -> Policy : Evaluate canonical host and key evidence

alt First use: no approved identity
  Policy --> Provider : trustRequired(full SHA-256, algorithm, generation)
  Provider --> App : Versioned bounded trust evidence
  Provider -> Provider : Stop safely before credential lookup
  App -> User : Show complete fingerprint and explicit actions
  alt User explicitly trusts
    User -> App : Approve reviewed identity
    App -> Profiles : Atomically publish generation + 1
    User -> App : Explicit retry
    App -> Provider : Start(new generation)
  else User cancels
    User -> App : Cancel
    App -> App : Keep profile untrusted and disconnected
  end
else Approved identity matches
  Policy --> Provider : approved(identity generation)
  Provider -> Keychain : Resolve opaque key/passphrase reference
  Keychain --> Provider : Bounded secret material
  Provider -> Host : Public-key authentication
  Host --> Provider : Authenticated session or typed rejection
else Changed, revoked, or lane-inconsistent identity
  Policy --> Provider : terminal identity mismatch
  Provider --> App : High-severity changed-key evidence
  Provider -> Provider : Stop before Keychain and authentication
  App -> User : Inspect old/new fingerprints; replace or cancel
end

note over Provider,Keychain
  The extension never waits indefinitely for foreground UI.
  Approval is durable; retry is a fresh explicit generation.
end note

@enduml